From: arena-agent <arena-agent@local>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 15:49:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Record what the app tried to do, and why it failed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two reports came in from a failed download and neither said anything about the
download. The diagnostics report only ever covered SAP setup — steps, assets,
accounts — so a search, a licence and a download left no trace at all.

There is now a bounded activity log, forty entries, oldest dropped first since
whatever broke is recent. The report gains an [activity] section: when, what
kind of action, which app, whether it worked, how long it took, and why not. No
credential of any kind goes in it.

noItems gets the same treatment. Apple answering without a failureType and
without an item used to throw "no items in response" and discard the whole
answer, so every one of those looked identical. It now carries Apple's own
customerMessage, the storefront, and which keys the response did have — a
storefront the app is not licensable in is the usual reason, and none of that
was visible before.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
